1
00:00:14,500 --> 00:00:27,330
Please contact us for any inquiries
turkision@gmail.com

2
00:02:03,707 --> 00:02:08,317
NO ANIMALS WERE HARMED DURING
THE FILMING OF THIS PRODUCTION

3
00:02:53,900 --> 00:02:57,900
What did you tell Geyhatu about me
Gündüz?

4
00:02:59,646 --> 00:03:03,216
Geyhatu is too scared to understand...

5
00:03:03,216 --> 00:03:07,046
...what I’m telling these days, Balgay.

6
00:03:09,398 --> 00:03:10,358
Speak up!

7
00:03:17,633 --> 00:03:20,393
I didn't know anything about your
business here...

8
00:03:20,393 --> 00:03:24,703
...neither your laws...

9
00:03:25,723 --> 00:03:27,073
...until...

10
00:03:30,034 --> 00:03:31,584
...your dog...

11
00:03:33,954 --> 00:03:37,624
...brought me here and tide me up.

12
00:05:12,267 --> 00:05:13,797
Allah!

13
00:05:17,309 --> 00:05:19,549
You will tell me everything.

14
00:05:22,172 --> 00:05:30,672
Know that I’ll cut you till your bones
are separated from your flesh.

15
00:05:33,422 --> 00:05:34,982
Soldiers are ready, Balgay.

16
00:06:03,634 --> 00:06:04,804
Any news from Longar?

17
00:06:05,034 --> 00:06:06,074
No, Balgay.

18
00:06:06,739 --> 00:06:08,329
He won’t return empty-handed.

19
00:06:11,153 --> 00:06:14,503
Make him speak till I’m back from
Kulucahisar.

20
00:06:29,358 --> 00:06:31,448
As you wish, Balgay.

21
00:06:48,298 --> 00:06:49,688
Commander Laskaris.

22
00:06:51,519 --> 00:06:54,559
Don’t return to castle unless you have
Sofia with you.

23
00:06:54,860 --> 00:06:56,210
Do you understand?

24
00:06:58,818 --> 00:07:01,588
Under the name of our Mother Mary...

25
00:07:01,588 --> 00:07:03,928
I swear I will find
the Princess, Master Yannis.

26
00:07:03,928 --> 00:07:09,325
Curse be on that day when the Mongols
and Turks came to our lands.

27
00:07:16,365 --> 00:07:18,465
Master Yannis, Osman Bey is here.

28
00:07:21,102 --> 00:07:22,002
Bring him.

29
00:07:45,318 --> 00:07:47,168
Osman!

30
00:08:25,472 --> 00:08:26,302
Sofia.

31
00:08:28,642 --> 00:08:30,372
Where is my daughter!?

32
00:08:31,251 --> 00:08:33,431
She showed me Selcan Hanim’s dagger...

33
00:08:34,011 --> 00:08:38,231
...to prove she has captured her when
she came back from Tent.

34
00:08:41,908 --> 00:08:44,778
I never forget, Yannis.

35
00:08:47,178 --> 00:08:48,238
I got your Sofia.

36
00:08:48,798 --> 00:08:50,328
What did you do to her?

37
00:08:50,328 --> 00:08:51,518
She has comfort.

38
00:08:53,250 --> 00:08:55,700
For now, she lays in her special cage like
a sheep.

39
00:08:55,700 --> 00:08:57,860
Waiting his father to save her.

40
00:08:58,150 --> 00:09:00,493
If you do anything to my daughter, I will-

41
00:09:00,563 --> 00:09:02,353
I came here to make an agreement.

42
00:09:04,649 --> 00:09:06,209
Only if you let me live...

43
00:09:07,867 --> 00:09:09,677
...Sofia will survive.

44
00:09:09,783 --> 00:09:11,333
What do you want from me? Osman!

45
00:09:11,563 --> 00:09:12,523
Balgay.

46
00:09:27,766 --> 00:09:28,666
Stop it!

47
00:09:31,630 --> 00:09:32,930
Don’t resist.

48
00:09:35,869 --> 00:09:38,149
You can’t treat me like this.

49
00:09:38,506 --> 00:09:39,666
Open my eyes!

50
00:09:41,086 --> 00:09:42,956
Open my eyes!

51
00:09:43,520 --> 00:09:44,370
Leave me!

52
00:09:51,262 --> 00:09:52,032
Open!

53
00:10:04,013 --> 00:10:05,823
Bala Hatun.

54
00:10:09,818 --> 00:10:11,178
It's our time now, Sofia.

55
00:10:17,695 --> 00:10:19,515
Andreas, Salvador and Helen...

56
00:10:21,559 --> 00:10:22,559
Where are they?

57
00:10:22,679 --> 00:10:24,669
You don't need to know that.

58
00:10:26,063 --> 00:10:28,443
I bring more important things.

59
00:10:29,542 --> 00:10:30,732
You like him so much…

60
00:10:32,552 --> 00:10:33,382
...my father.

61
00:10:37,800 --> 00:10:38,960
Sheikh Edebali.

62
00:10:40,246 --> 00:10:43,786
He is gathering up valiants and Ahis who
are willing to fight.

63
00:10:46,343 --> 00:10:49,433
Osman Bey has very plans no mind
can understand.

64
00:10:52,955 --> 00:10:56,855
You do not see the fire burning in
front of you and armies who...

65
00:10:56,855 --> 00:10:59,415
...carry wood to that fire.

66
00:11:01,630 --> 00:11:02,670
It’s a shame.

67
00:11:13,583 --> 00:11:16,003
This hyena need a more powerful collar.

68
00:11:19,877 --> 00:11:21,747
Untie her, Zulfikar Dervish.

69
00:11:42,391 --> 00:11:43,561
Zulfikar Dervish!

70
00:11:45,214 --> 00:11:46,184
Leave.

71
00:11:49,460 --> 00:11:50,380
Leave!

72
00:12:20,926 --> 00:12:22,416
It won't happen, Bala.

73
00:12:24,468 --> 00:12:27,948
Whether I'm alive or not, your
end is certain.

74
00:12:31,325 --> 00:12:33,195
You will vanish!

75
00:12:49,803 --> 00:12:54,513
You better stop taunting and show what
you are capable of.

76
00:13:20,691 --> 00:13:22,071
Now you see.

77
00:13:24,377 --> 00:13:25,537
Little girl!

78
00:13:37,932 --> 00:13:39,522
You slaughtered Ahi Evren.

79
00:13:41,852 --> 00:13:43,022
Sheikhl Edebali.

80
00:13:43,189 --> 00:13:44,119
Hakça.

81
00:13:44,874 --> 00:13:45,794
Pehlivan.

82
00:13:45,794 --> 00:13:46,704
Zulfikar.

83
00:13:46,704 --> 00:13:47,564
Gonca...

84
00:13:47,564 --> 00:13:48,514
Dervishes...

85
00:13:48,514 --> 00:13:50,794
Ahis... All of them came. Sofia!

86
00:13:57,611 --> 00:14:00,771
And Osman Bey!

87
00:14:39,008 --> 00:14:40,618
Remember this day, Bala.

88
00:14:41,409 --> 00:14:44,409
I never forget, Sofia. You remember!

89
00:14:44,923 --> 00:14:47,123
Remember this moment.

90
00:15:24,750 --> 00:15:26,360
Are you okay, Bala Hatun?

91
00:15:39,352 --> 00:15:43,272
If I hand Balgay to you, Geyhatu will
raze this castle upon us.

92
00:15:43,673 --> 00:15:46,453
Sooner or later, you know it is going to
happen to you.

93
00:15:46,523 --> 00:15:50,193
I get along with Balgay.
Why should I betray him?

94
00:15:50,605 --> 00:15:52,925
You are just playing games to each other.

95
00:15:54,955 --> 00:15:57,115
Who do you think is going to win
at the end?

96
00:15:57,448 --> 00:15:58,258
You?

97
00:15:59,052 --> 00:15:59,922
Or Balgay?

98
00:16:02,916 --> 00:16:06,276
One of you will try to kill the other once
there is an opportunity.

99
00:16:08,294 --> 00:16:12,294
I’m the only one who can save you
and my Tent from Balgay.

100
00:16:12,294 --> 00:16:13,504
And then?

101
00:16:15,548 --> 00:16:19,148
Flood goes, sand stays. Yannis.

102
00:16:20,291 --> 00:16:29,211
Then we will face you and your daughter
along with the demonic powers behind you.

103
00:16:31,465 --> 00:16:32,895
Either you!

104
00:16:34,156 --> 00:16:35,386
Or us!

105
00:16:47,721 --> 00:16:48,445
Speak.

106
00:16:48,445 --> 00:16:49,645
I’m listening.

107
00:16:51,520 --> 00:16:52,690
Tomorrow…

108
00:16:53,312 --> 00:16:55,982
You will convince Balgay to go to
İnegöl's governor.

109
00:16:56,629 --> 00:17:02,179
He'll be convinced that he'll take the
castle and chests full of gold.

110
00:17:05,088 --> 00:17:08,498
I know which route Balgay is
going to take...

111
00:17:08,498 --> 00:17:11,428
...after his soldiers leave their camp
site.

112
00:17:11,428 --> 00:17:14,728
And you will ambush them. Is that it?

113
00:17:15,474 --> 00:17:17,694
Both of us will get rid Balgay.

114
00:17:19,102 --> 00:17:21,652
Only with a bunch of Alps...

115
00:17:21,652 --> 00:17:24,612
You don’t have chance against his
soldiers.

116
00:17:25,397 --> 00:17:26,627
It’s my problem.

117
00:17:27,689 --> 00:17:29,449
Let’s say you killed Balgay.

118
00:17:32,117 --> 00:17:37,517
How can I be sure that you will free
my daughter once you are done.

119
00:17:38,134 --> 00:17:39,604
I give you my word.

120
00:17:39,614 --> 00:17:41,764
The son of Ertugrul Ghazi, Osman Bey.

121
00:17:44,231 --> 00:17:45,211
Soldiers!

122
00:17:54,496 --> 00:17:57,786
Being trustworthy and hostileness
are different topics.

123
00:17:59,274 --> 00:18:02,294
I can trust you but sometimes...

124
00:18:03,194 --> 00:18:06,894
...being trustworthy does not work like
that.

125
00:18:07,132 --> 00:18:09,272
For our alliance...

126
00:18:27,117 --> 00:18:29,777
...I present you the Laws of Genghis Khan.

127
00:18:30,661 --> 00:18:34,661
You will hold it until I’m here
with your daughter..

128
00:18:37,038 --> 00:18:39,448
What if you will be the one who dies?

129
00:18:44,372 --> 00:18:45,942
Laws of Genghis Khan...

130
00:18:50,082 --> 00:18:52,282
...are more important than Sofia for us.

131
00:18:56,463 --> 00:19:01,463
You will give the laws and take
your daughter back when the time comes.

132
00:19:01,603 --> 00:19:02,923
That’s it.

133
00:19:05,477 --> 00:19:13,547
What if I sacrifice my daughter for
the laws and your life?

134
00:19:13,847 --> 00:19:17,825
We both know how bad you want to make
Sofia the Princess of Constantinople.

135
00:19:17,835 --> 00:19:18,825
Yannis.

136
00:19:19,647 --> 00:19:22,157
You are nothing without Sofia.

137
00:19:35,104 --> 00:19:36,524
What will happen now, my Bey?

138
00:19:36,614 --> 00:19:38,054
May I come in, my Bey?

139
00:19:38,532 --> 00:19:39,682
You shall come in.

140
00:19:43,665 --> 00:19:44,405
Relax.

141
00:19:44,405 --> 00:19:45,435
What happened to you?

142
00:19:45,645 --> 00:19:48,155
We can’t be relaxed during times like
these, Efendi!

143
00:19:48,191 --> 00:19:49,121
Something…

144
00:19:49,181 --> 00:19:51,061
...something happened to Gunduz.

145
00:19:51,061 --> 00:19:52,081
Tell us now.

146
00:19:52,312 --> 00:19:53,022
My Bey.

147
00:19:53,179 --> 00:19:55,249
We found two Alps of Gunduz Bey.

148
00:19:55,262 --> 00:19:56,322
They are dead.

149
00:19:56,648 --> 00:19:58,338
No traces from Gunduz Bey.

150
00:19:58,338 --> 00:19:59,458
Who killed them?

151
00:19:59,458 --> 00:20:00,778
We don’t know, my Bey.

152
00:20:00,778 --> 00:20:02,598
Why did Gunduz leave the Tent?

153
00:20:02,598 --> 00:20:03,758
Where was he going?

154
00:20:03,758 --> 00:20:06,558
He left because he wanted to find
Osman and join him.

155
00:20:09,582 --> 00:20:12,752
And now you are making
decisions about battles?

156
00:20:13,282 --> 00:20:17,192
Do you think our war is different than
theirs?

157
00:20:17,282 --> 00:20:19,522
Yes, it’s indeed different.

158
00:20:20,122 --> 00:20:22,942
After Bey of Kayi chose to cooperate
with the Mongols.

159
00:20:22,942 --> 00:20:24,652
Of course it’s different.

160
00:20:24,652 --> 00:20:26,472
And it means our battle is different!

161
00:20:27,547 --> 00:20:33,787
Then, why did you ran to my door and asked
for my help in times of need?

162
00:20:34,371 --> 00:20:36,851
Why didn’t you ask for help from Osman?

163
00:20:37,338 --> 00:20:38,088
Huh?

164
00:20:38,720 --> 00:20:40,470
Osman is a fugitive.

165
00:20:41,336 --> 00:20:43,986
You can’t find him if you look for him...

166
00:20:43,986 --> 00:20:47,226
...and you can’t hold him even if you find
him.

167
00:20:48,484 --> 00:20:54,934
So when you are in trouble you ask help
from a Bey you don’t obey.

168
00:20:56,967 --> 00:21:00,267
Take a look at yourselves.

169
00:21:00,747 --> 00:21:06,827
Remember well from which door
the followers of Osman Bey seek help.

170
00:21:07,355 --> 00:21:08,395
Remember well.

171
00:21:09,852 --> 00:21:12,972
Tell Alps to search the area.

172
00:21:20,516 --> 00:21:21,996
What are you up to? My Bey.

173
00:21:22,011 --> 00:21:23,041
Where are you going?

174
00:21:23,394 --> 00:21:24,644
I need to see Balgay.

175
00:21:26,641 --> 00:21:28,291
Gunduz went after Osman.

176
00:21:28,741 --> 00:21:30,281
What can Balgay do?

177
00:21:32,282 --> 00:21:33,982
Don’t drag him into this.

178
00:21:34,112 --> 00:21:36,052
Mongols are everywhere, Hatun.

179
00:21:37,031 --> 00:21:39,741
They may know something about them.

180
00:21:40,168 --> 00:21:41,638
We shall go and find out.

181
00:21:42,116 --> 00:21:43,096
Batur!

182
00:21:43,914 --> 00:21:45,394
Come with me, my son.

183
00:21:46,891 --> 00:21:48,771
Take good care of yourselves.

184
00:22:28,230 --> 00:22:29,370
Osman Bey!

185
00:22:50,033 --> 00:22:51,103
Brothers!

186
00:22:51,581 --> 00:22:52,671
My Osman!

187
00:22:53,251 --> 00:22:54,981
What have you been up to, my Osman?

188
00:22:55,030 --> 00:22:56,920
Yannis accepted my proposal.

189
00:22:58,057 --> 00:23:00,107
We will ambush Balgay.

190
00:23:01,226 --> 00:23:05,476
Finally, the time has come.
He'll pay for what he has done.

191
00:23:06,121 --> 00:23:08,481
What do you want to do, Osman Bey?
Taking Balgay?

192
00:23:08,481 --> 00:23:11,001
No. Taking his life!

193
00:23:13,665 --> 00:23:18,735
We'll show him how being
cruel ends awfully.

194
00:23:20,319 --> 00:23:22,679
Balgay and his followers will see that...

195
00:23:23,465 --> 00:23:27,225
... mighty trees grow in stormy lands.

196
00:23:28,852 --> 00:23:33,252
If they try to cut our branches off, we'll
pull their roots out!

197
00:23:34,182 --> 00:23:38,182
Praise be! Allahu Akbar!

198
00:23:38,818 --> 00:23:42,488
- Allahu Akbar!
- Allahu Akbar!

199
00:23:57,455 --> 00:24:00,265
My Bey! Gündüz Bey!

200
00:24:01,542 --> 00:24:03,102
What happened to my brother?

201
00:24:03,102 --> 00:24:06,122
They kidnapped Gündüz Bey!
They are looking for him everywhere.

202
00:24:06,122 --> 00:24:08,072
What are you saying, Erkut?

203
00:24:29,406 --> 00:24:30,846
Balgay!

204
00:24:31,960 --> 00:24:33,770
Balgay!

205
00:24:41,517 --> 00:24:43,527
Balgay did this.

206
00:24:54,734 --> 00:24:57,994
He wants to know who informed Geyhatu.

207
00:24:59,785 --> 00:25:01,405
He'll see.

208
00:25:03,294 --> 00:25:07,144
Come on valiants, come on!
We're going to Balgay's Tent.

209
00:25:07,780 --> 00:25:11,000
My Bey! Shouldn't we wait for the night?

210
00:25:11,000 --> 00:25:15,240
Balgay is going to the castle now.
He's probably keeping my brother in the base.

211
00:25:15,675 --> 00:25:17,645
Now is the right time. Let's go!

212
00:25:22,446 --> 00:25:25,196
Konur. You stay here.

213
00:25:26,837 --> 00:25:28,807
It's just a scratch, my Bey.

214
00:25:31,519 --> 00:25:33,459
Make this dog talk.

215
00:25:33,952 --> 00:25:36,102
He's the one who killed Köni.

216
00:25:37,339 --> 00:25:39,819
We must learn about Balgay's tricks.

217
00:25:40,364 --> 00:25:44,084
The information we'll take to Geyhatu
will be his end.

218
00:25:44,462 --> 00:25:45,812
Let's go.

219
00:25:51,408 --> 00:25:55,038
Keep an eye on him.

220
00:25:55,662 --> 00:25:57,292
I will, my Bey.

221
00:26:40,481 --> 00:26:43,491
What tricks are you playing? Tell me.

222
00:26:43,736 --> 00:26:45,436
Enough with that, Hatun.

223
00:26:45,709 --> 00:26:49,009
You said you were sending clothes
to Batur...

224
00:26:50,091 --> 00:26:52,631
... and they ambushed Bala.

225
00:26:52,631 --> 00:26:56,811
Now Gündüz was attacked out of nowhere.

226
00:26:57,448 --> 00:26:59,948
Tell me! Why?

227
00:27:00,681 --> 00:27:03,091
Who is behind all of this?

228
00:27:03,091 --> 00:27:04,921
- Enough!
- It's not enough!

229
00:27:04,921 --> 00:27:11,881
If you're involved in these, I'll scratch
your eyes out, know that, Zöhre!

230
00:27:11,881 --> 00:27:14,611
What are you implying, Hatun?

231
00:27:14,611 --> 00:27:18,681
What I'm implying isn't important.

232
00:27:18,681 --> 00:27:23,241
What's important is your concern
which you fail to hide.

233
00:27:49,250 --> 00:27:51,710
What did you do to Sofia?

234
00:27:51,808 --> 00:27:53,808
She looked like she had been through hell.

235
00:27:53,808 --> 00:27:55,468
She deserved it.

236
00:27:55,910 --> 00:28:00,010
Do you give everyone
what they deserve, Bala?

237
00:28:05,524 --> 00:28:08,224
Give Osman Bey what he deserves, Bala.

238
00:28:08,224 --> 00:28:11,984
Your love isn't from the vanishing kind.

239
00:28:13,865 --> 00:28:16,455
I thought about it a lot, Gonca.

240
00:28:18,200 --> 00:28:23,310
If I marry Osman while I'm in a situation
like this, that would be unfair to him.

241
00:28:23,310 --> 00:28:26,200
It wouldn't, my Bala. It wouldn't.

242
00:28:26,458 --> 00:28:30,088
It wouldn't be unfair if you talk to
Osman Bey about it.

243
00:28:30,832 --> 00:28:33,522
I wouldn't marry him without
telling him, of course.

244
00:28:34,167 --> 00:28:36,107
It's not about that.

245
00:28:37,129 --> 00:28:39,799
Osman wouldn't give up even If I told him.

246
00:28:41,679 --> 00:28:43,959
He wouldn't let his love go.

247
00:28:48,265 --> 00:28:49,715
Then...

248
00:28:50,753 --> 00:28:52,823
.. he'll want a child.

249
00:28:55,415 --> 00:28:56,855
He will.

250
00:28:57,623 --> 00:28:59,023
It's his right.

251
00:29:03,324 --> 00:29:08,834
Then he'll either find another Hatun,
or he'll accept life without children.

252
00:29:09,994 --> 00:29:12,534
What happens to us then, Gonca?

253
00:30:32,326 --> 00:30:34,226
Talk, Gündüz!

254
00:30:40,896 --> 00:30:43,766
What did you tell Geyhatu, Gündüz?

255
00:30:45,826 --> 00:30:49,506
Did you tell Geyhatu that
Balgay had the laws?

256
00:31:01,279 --> 00:31:04,259
So Balgay is...

257
00:31:05,160 --> 00:31:09,280
... playing tricks on Geyhatu, huh?

258
00:31:21,057 --> 00:31:24,687
If I were you I would talk
before Balgay comes.

259
00:31:24,878 --> 00:31:27,248
Think about what he'll do to you.

260
00:31:30,647 --> 00:31:32,127
Talk!

261
00:31:45,244 --> 00:31:46,864
Cerkutay!

262
00:31:48,445 --> 00:31:51,405
Take my life.

263
00:31:51,767 --> 00:31:56,277
Or I will make you pay for this!

264
00:31:58,948 --> 00:32:00,478
Remember that!

265
00:32:01,309 --> 00:32:03,379
Take my life!

266
00:32:10,612 --> 00:32:13,312
Your death won't be easy, Gündüz!

267
00:32:14,951 --> 00:32:16,881
But I won't be the one who'll do it.

268
00:32:18,106 --> 00:32:19,926
Balgay will be.

269
00:32:22,303 --> 00:32:26,303
In agony, slowly!

270
00:32:50,728 --> 00:32:53,698
Gündüz Bey! May Allah help you!

271
00:33:16,743 --> 00:33:22,283
Bey! They tied Gündüz Bey up.
That dog Cerkutay is torturing him.

272
00:33:24,558 --> 00:33:27,828
That dog who injured Bala is also here.

273
00:33:30,485 --> 00:33:33,125
He thinks it was my brother
who informed Geyhatu.

274
00:33:33,125 --> 00:33:36,395
And Gündüz Bey is not telling him
anything so the Tent is safe.

275
00:33:38,472 --> 00:33:41,082
- You should watch the road.
- Okay, my Bey.

276
00:33:43,641 --> 00:33:45,171
Listen closely.

277
00:33:46,054 --> 00:33:49,814
There are guards all over the base.

278
00:33:57,989 --> 00:34:00,529
Balgay's units are on patrol.

279
00:34:08,405 --> 00:34:10,565
There are 80 soldiers in Söğüt.

280
00:34:10,565 --> 00:34:12,765
Almost that many went to the castle.

281
00:34:16,466 --> 00:34:19,206
There are too many soldiers in the base.

282
00:34:19,534 --> 00:34:22,344
We'll suddenly be all over them.

283
00:34:35,940 --> 00:34:39,940
Samsa Bey, your Alps will go in from
the East and the West.

284
00:34:39,940 --> 00:34:42,670
Thank my Allah for keeping my blade sharp!

285
00:34:43,687 --> 00:34:46,557
- Let's go then, valiants.
- Let's go.

286
00:35:30,574 --> 00:35:36,124
I can't see the governors.
Where are they, Yannis?

287
00:35:36,124 --> 00:35:43,614
They came. They said that they
will obey you and brought their gifts.

288
00:35:44,593 --> 00:35:50,083
I said, where are they, Yannis?

289
00:35:56,414 --> 00:35:58,854
I sent them all back.

290
00:36:02,013 --> 00:36:06,353
Look at me, old man. Are you playing
tricks on Balgay?

291
00:36:10,955 --> 00:36:12,415
Osman!

292
00:36:13,686 --> 00:36:15,356
What about him?

293
00:36:15,601 --> 00:36:18,161
He caught my daughter Sofia.

294
00:36:19,043 --> 00:36:21,033
Where is Osman?

295
00:36:22,178 --> 00:36:24,248
He was just here.

296
00:36:29,399 --> 00:36:32,269
Osman came all the way to here...

297
00:36:34,076 --> 00:36:36,496
... and you let him go?

298
00:36:37,105 --> 00:36:43,125
Remember! He has my daughter and
your Queen!

299
00:36:53,421 --> 00:36:57,561
What did he ask from you in
exchange for Sofia?

300
00:36:59,520 --> 00:37:00,700
You.

301
00:37:03,046 --> 00:37:08,356
He asked for your life in exchange
for my daughter's life.

302
00:37:15,617 --> 00:37:17,187
What did you say?

303
00:37:20,595 --> 00:37:23,935
"If I kill Balgay while he's in
my castle"...

304
00:37:25,554 --> 00:37:28,544
... "Geyhatu would destroy our castle".

305
00:37:32,336 --> 00:37:34,016
You're right.

306
00:37:40,001 --> 00:37:43,821
What did Osman say?

307
00:37:44,065 --> 00:37:48,985
"I will do it. You just bring him to me
and I'll give you your daughter."

308
00:37:51,179 --> 00:37:55,869
Where will you take me and
give me to Osman?

309
00:37:56,178 --> 00:38:02,118
I told him that you'll go to İnegöl's
governor and take his taxes.

310
00:38:02,398 --> 00:38:06,698
He said he'll be setting up a trap
in the gate.

311
00:38:09,508 --> 00:38:10,918
Good.

312
00:38:12,123 --> 00:38:16,553
You will bring Osman back to me
so I can get my daughter, Balgay!

313
00:38:18,324 --> 00:38:25,944
If my daughter dies, your dreams of
Constantinople dies with her, know that!

314
00:40:05,592 --> 00:40:06,902
Osman!

315
00:40:39,422 --> 00:40:41,462
They are Balgay's prisoners!

316
00:40:47,544 --> 00:40:49,054
Osman!

317
00:40:55,685 --> 00:40:58,475
What did you do, brother?

318
00:41:00,035 --> 00:41:04,315
Are you out of your mind, brother?

319
00:41:05,945 --> 00:41:07,825
What are you doing here?

320
00:41:11,799 --> 00:41:12,839
Brother!

321
00:41:15,366 --> 00:41:18,506
Are you okay, brother?

322
00:41:18,777 --> 00:41:21,947
I had hope until you came.

323
00:41:28,049 --> 00:41:29,759
Now it's gone.

324
00:41:54,576 --> 00:41:56,316
Sergeant Samsa.

325
00:42:08,543 --> 00:42:09,293
Bamsı!

326
00:42:22,195 --> 00:42:23,275
Osman!

327
00:42:40,150 --> 00:42:43,600
I knew you would do something
insane for your brother but...

328
00:42:43,600 --> 00:42:45,820
... I didn't expect this insane.

329
00:42:46,203 --> 00:42:49,153
You can't even say the word bravery!

330
00:42:49,804 --> 00:42:54,204
You're only brave towards women and
tied men!

331
00:42:58,064 --> 00:43:00,704
Bala Hatun escaped from me.

332
00:43:03,429 --> 00:43:05,879
But you won't be able to.

333
00:43:08,933 --> 00:43:10,953
You'll die with your brother!

334
00:43:15,495 --> 00:43:19,275
You came to Balgay's hell by yourself.

335
00:43:26,984 --> 00:43:28,964
Hang them to the hooks.

336
00:43:29,319 --> 00:43:33,319
They will stay there until
they are torn to shreds.

337
00:43:35,089 --> 00:43:38,299
We'll have a feast when Balgay comes here!

338
00:43:38,567 --> 00:43:43,897
- Balgay!
- Balgay!

339
00:43:45,534 --> 00:43:48,944
I'll give you such a feast...

340
00:43:49,552 --> 00:43:52,382
... that you won't be able to get
enough of your own flesh!

341
00:43:52,755 --> 00:43:56,375
Instead of kumys, I'll make you
drink your own blood!

342
00:44:01,344 --> 00:44:03,664
Hang Osman first.

343
00:44:14,613 --> 00:44:18,023
Freedom or death!

344
00:44:30,512 --> 00:44:35,042
- Allahu Akbar!
- Allahu Akbar!

345
00:44:39,680 --> 00:44:41,770
Like a wall.

346
00:44:42,189 --> 00:44:44,409
Good thing we came prepared.

347
00:44:56,094 --> 00:44:58,124
Allahu Akbar!

348
00:44:58,667 --> 00:45:00,477
Get them, valiants!

349
00:45:01,212 --> 00:45:02,032
AllahuAkbar!

350
00:45:02,215 --> 00:45:03,705
Hit them for the sake of Allah.

351
00:45:03,846 --> 00:45:05,236
Don't let them!

352
00:45:05,847 --> 00:45:07,897
AllahuAkbar!

353
00:45:09,904 --> 00:45:11,434
Arrows.

354
00:45:18,044 --> 00:45:19,984
Hit them!

355
00:45:33,425 --> 00:45:34,695
Allah!

356
00:45:47,188 --> 00:45:48,288
Osman.

357
00:45:48,993 --> 00:45:51,583
He is more overbold than I expect,
Alisar Bey.

358
00:45:52,163 --> 00:45:56,163
Till now, no one could break into the
headquarters of Balgay.

359
00:45:56,223 --> 00:45:57,963
Yes he is, Melik.

360
00:45:58,347 --> 00:46:00,547
He is such a overbold man that...

361
00:46:00,810 --> 00:46:04,810
He is blinfolded enough to not see the
trouble approaching to him.

362
00:46:04,937 --> 00:46:07,337
When Geyhatu hears what happened...

363
00:46:07,414 --> 00:46:10,214
...he will dig Balgay's grave with
his own hands, my bey.

364
00:46:10,320 --> 00:46:11,810
Till that beautiful day...

365
00:46:12,387 --> 00:46:15,327
... I'll try to bury Osman and dündar.

366
00:46:16,401 --> 00:46:19,601
We came here to carry soil to
the grave of our enemies.

367
00:46:19,922 --> 00:46:21,882
Luckily...

368
00:46:23,433 --> 00:46:27,433
Our enemies try to bury each other
before us.

369
00:47:01,194 --> 00:47:02,324
Brother.

370
00:47:20,056 --> 00:47:21,056
Brother.

371
00:47:21,139 --> 00:47:22,769
Stay strong, my brother.

372
00:47:29,932 --> 00:47:31,272
Osman!

373
00:47:45,545 --> 00:47:46,925
Ah!

374
00:47:50,014 --> 00:47:51,114
Are you okay?

375
00:47:51,134 --> 00:47:52,164
I'm fine, brother.

376
00:47:52,164 --> 00:47:53,054
I'm fine.

377
00:47:57,103 --> 00:47:58,833
Bamsi bey.

378
00:47:59,045 --> 00:48:00,525
Protect my brother.

379
00:48:17,863 --> 00:48:19,293
Melik.

380
00:48:19,423 --> 00:48:20,903
Take out foods from bag.

381
00:48:20,986 --> 00:48:22,976
We'll enjoy the view.

382
00:48:23,436 --> 00:48:25,536
Let's watch the rumble.

383
00:48:26,945 --> 00:48:28,025
My bey.

384
00:48:57,592 --> 00:48:58,622
Braves...

385
00:48:58,761 --> 00:49:01,011
...fight truly,Cerkutay

386
00:49:02,003 --> 00:49:03,673
You do the dirty...

387
00:49:04,083 --> 00:49:06,223
...when you see a brave man.

388
00:49:06,451 --> 00:49:08,081
Let's see you.

389
00:49:09,785 --> 00:49:13,955
Look at the taste of my sword
which killed a lot lof Kayı.

390
00:49:14,158 --> 00:49:15,518
Come here!

391
00:49:15,749 --> 00:49:17,629
Come to your death!

392
00:49:18,148 --> 00:49:19,428
Come...

393
00:49:19,520 --> 00:49:23,520
....to pay the cost of all the
young men you've killed.

394
00:49:40,492 --> 00:49:43,002
That's for Balgay.

395
00:49:49,021 --> 00:49:51,241
That's for my brother.

396
00:49:57,077 --> 00:50:00,117
That's for all young men.

397
00:50:30,082 --> 00:50:32,692
I'm not done with you, Cerkutay.

398
00:50:32,981 --> 00:50:34,301
I'm not.

399
00:50:41,920 --> 00:50:43,650
Hit them, guys!

400
00:51:13,688 --> 00:51:15,698
We've crossed the snowy mountains.

401
00:51:15,778 --> 00:51:18,298
We've become a strong lizard, Bamsi bey.

402
00:51:18,448 --> 00:51:20,628
We attacked to headquarters, Samsa bey.

403
00:51:20,718 --> 00:51:21,848
Well done.

404
00:51:22,275 --> 00:51:23,365
Brother.

405
00:51:28,752 --> 00:51:29,742
Osman.

406
00:51:29,954 --> 00:51:32,094
There are important things.

407
00:51:32,256 --> 00:51:34,216
We need to hurry.

408
00:51:34,268 --> 00:51:36,438
Let's go before Balgay comes.

409
00:51:42,177 --> 00:51:43,297
Erkut.

410
00:51:44,027 --> 00:51:45,027
Erkut.

411
00:51:46,937 --> 00:51:47,747
My bey.

412
00:51:47,885 --> 00:51:49,755
Dundar bey and Batur bey are coming.

413
00:51:49,865 --> 00:51:51,795
They have our horses with them.

414
00:52:15,149 --> 00:52:16,089
Erkut.

415
00:52:16,806 --> 00:52:18,146
Take Gunduz bey.

416
00:52:18,275 --> 00:52:19,165
Osman.

417
00:52:19,586 --> 00:52:20,546
Never...

418
00:52:20,799 --> 00:52:22,399
...do this, my brother.

419
00:52:24,210 --> 00:52:26,670
Go before Balgay comes, my brother.

420
00:52:29,109 --> 00:52:31,299
There's something you don't know

421
00:53:07,367 --> 00:53:09,927
Dundar Bey.

422
00:53:28,120 --> 00:53:30,980
You are the only one who
gives the cure, my Allah.

423
00:53:32,414 --> 00:53:33,804
Brother.

424
00:53:39,340 --> 00:53:40,570
My brother.

425
00:53:40,862 --> 00:53:42,002
Are you okay?

426
00:53:44,518 --> 00:53:47,728
I don't feel anything because of
my heart's pain, brother.

427
00:53:48,683 --> 00:53:50,183
All will be well, my brother.

428
00:53:50,296 --> 00:53:51,296
All...

429
00:53:51,973 --> 00:53:53,903
We'll come through it.

430
00:53:55,623 --> 00:53:57,863
How couldn't I realize anything
till now?

431
00:54:01,037 --> 00:54:03,207
How I've done these to you?

432
00:54:04,737 --> 00:54:06,087
Goktug.

433
00:54:06,912 --> 00:54:08,772
You shouldn't look at the
starting...

434
00:54:08,772 --> 00:54:09,912
...but ending.

435
00:54:10,377 --> 00:54:11,297
Look.

436
00:54:11,568 --> 00:54:13,238
The result is good.

437
00:54:13,348 --> 00:54:14,958
We've came together.

438
00:54:15,064 --> 00:54:17,164
That's the important thing.

439
00:54:17,705 --> 00:54:18,625
I wish....

440
00:54:19,549 --> 00:54:22,679
I wish we had a father and a mother...

441
00:54:22,760 --> 00:54:25,300
...and they saw us like this, brother.

442
00:54:26,441 --> 00:54:28,241
They didn't , my brother.

443
00:54:28,777 --> 00:54:31,177
They didn't allow us to live it.

444
00:54:31,787 --> 00:54:33,827
They've destroyed our tents...

445
00:54:35,391 --> 00:54:36,521
...father...

446
00:54:37,093 --> 00:54:38,583
...mother.

447
00:54:42,117 --> 00:54:43,787
But don't worry.

448
00:54:44,256 --> 00:54:46,106
Everything will be allright.

449
00:54:46,126 --> 00:54:47,806
How will that be, my brother?

450
00:54:48,713 --> 00:54:50,573
How?

451
00:54:50,624 --> 00:54:52,424
I've killed a lot of people.

452
00:54:52,593 --> 00:54:54,383
I've been a cruel.

453
00:54:55,064 --> 00:54:57,264
Will Osman bey forgive me?

454
00:54:58,248 --> 00:55:00,238
Osman bey is merciful...

455
00:55:00,421 --> 00:55:02,171
...as much as he is fair.

456
00:55:03,839 --> 00:55:05,099
Wait a little bit.

457
00:55:05,189 --> 00:55:07,219
We will wait till you are calm.

458
00:55:07,713 --> 00:55:09,373
Then he will understand us surely...

459
00:55:09,442 --> 00:55:10,862
...when we explain it.

460
00:55:14,626 --> 00:55:15,876
Balgay.

461
00:55:16,084 --> 00:55:18,614
Balgay won't stop following us.

462
00:55:19,139 --> 00:55:20,379
I know him.

463
00:55:20,647 --> 00:55:22,097
He won't accept it.

464
00:55:22,892 --> 00:55:26,612
Even if Balgay tries to attack me...

465
00:55:26,742 --> 00:55:28,582
..with all Mongols...

466
00:55:28,863 --> 00:55:30,973
...I will not allow him to take you.

467
00:55:36,389 --> 00:55:38,969
We've forgotten your wound
because of brother longing.

468
00:55:40,719 --> 00:55:42,959
I'll bring some ointment for you.

469
00:55:43,685 --> 00:55:45,575
I'll put it on your wound.

470
00:55:47,668 --> 00:55:49,548
My brother...

471
00:56:59,484 --> 00:57:00,734
Father

472
00:57:01,428 --> 00:57:03,318
What happened here?

473
00:57:09,748 --> 00:57:10,858
May Allah...

474
00:57:11,964 --> 00:57:14,914
...protect us from what
I think, my son.

475
00:57:15,553 --> 00:57:16,683
Osman...

476
00:57:18,404 --> 00:57:20,404
How he could do this?

477
00:57:20,850 --> 00:57:22,340
It seems that...

478
00:57:22,734 --> 00:57:24,734
...the soldiers of Samsar...

479
00:57:24,800 --> 00:57:26,650
...entered his service.

480
00:57:28,844 --> 00:57:31,234
How long will itl continue, father?

481
00:57:31,421 --> 00:57:33,331
We need to stop Osman.

482
00:57:33,491 --> 00:57:35,921
Either we'll stop him...

483
00:57:36,683 --> 00:57:40,313
...or the anger of the Balgay ...

484
00:57:40,503 --> 00:57:41,503
will hit us.

485
00:58:16,622 --> 00:58:17,682
Osman!

486
00:59:27,470 --> 00:59:29,900
You were the same when you're young.

487
00:59:30,411 --> 00:59:32,581
You used to speak a lot...

488
00:59:32,832 --> 00:59:34,742
when you hurt yourself.

489
00:59:39,571 --> 00:59:42,391
Mongol guy scared me a lot, my brother.

490
00:59:43,984 --> 00:59:46,184
I hardly remember those days.

491
00:59:50,508 --> 00:59:52,028
Goktug.

492
00:59:52,254 --> 00:59:54,384
As we've came together...

493
00:59:55,114 --> 00:59:57,394
...nothing will happen to you from now on.

494
01:00:05,653 --> 01:00:06,613
Is it okey?

495
01:00:06,673 --> 01:00:08,143
Yes, brother.

496
01:00:14,400 --> 01:00:15,870
I won't get bored.

497
01:00:16,070 --> 01:00:18,110
I will tell everything to you.

498
01:00:18,207 --> 01:00:19,497
I will tell you our mother...

499
01:00:19,517 --> 01:00:20,397
...father...

500
01:00:20,427 --> 01:00:21,667
...our tent...

501
01:00:21,757 --> 01:00:24,417
and even
our wars with tahtakilic.

502
01:00:25,694 --> 01:00:27,374
I will teach all.

503
01:00:27,719 --> 01:00:30,229
I won't leave you ever after the moment

504
01:00:30,980 --> 01:00:33,110
I held your hand, my brother.

505
01:00:33,201 --> 01:00:35,171
Thank you, my brother.

506
01:00:35,365 --> 01:00:37,135
Thanks!

507
01:00:37,625 --> 01:00:38,965
My brother.

508
01:00:45,940 --> 01:00:50,760
You've done this eventually Osman, huh?

509
01:00:51,301 --> 01:00:53,001
Now...

510
01:00:53,464 --> 01:00:56,634
Who will save you from Balgay's hand?

511
01:00:56,903 --> 01:01:00,473
Who will save you from me, Dündar Bey?

512
01:01:01,793 --> 01:01:03,083
What happened?

513
01:01:03,674 --> 01:01:06,464
Do you fear that your boss who
rules you will get angry?

514
01:01:09,279 --> 01:01:10,609
Batur!

515
01:01:17,425 --> 01:01:18,855
Stop, my son.

516
01:01:22,184 --> 01:01:24,724
He signed his own death warrant.

517
01:01:25,904 --> 01:01:28,684
You don't kill your brother.

518
01:01:30,266 --> 01:01:33,026
If I don't take the revenge
of Suleyman Sah...

519
01:01:33,219 --> 01:01:34,769
...from you...

520
01:01:35,263 --> 01:01:40,053
...don't call me as the son of the
Ertugrul Gazi bey anymore.

521
01:01:45,790 --> 01:01:47,620
Where is Gündüz?

522
01:01:47,735 --> 01:01:49,615
I saved my brother from them.

523
01:01:49,790 --> 01:01:51,440
What's it to you?

524
01:01:53,918 --> 01:01:56,238
What they wanted from your brother?

525
01:01:56,275 --> 01:01:59,145
They wanted their trouble and
got what they wanted.

526
01:01:59,168 --> 01:02:03,168
Now, it's your turn.

527
01:02:03,913 --> 01:02:05,993
Ah, Osman!

528
01:02:05,993 --> 01:02:07,097
Ah!

529
01:02:09,490 --> 01:02:12,290
What will I do with you?

530
01:02:16,161 --> 01:02:18,791
You've done what you wanted.

531
01:02:19,830 --> 01:02:23,350
You sold my father's throne
to Mongols.

532
01:02:23,914 --> 01:02:25,794
Then you settled on it.

533
01:02:26,396 --> 01:02:28,436
I've done it for our tent.

534
01:02:28,816 --> 01:02:30,856
I've done it for you.

535
01:02:31,218 --> 01:02:33,558
I've done it to save the life of...

536
01:02:33,614 --> 01:02:37,084
...those brave people who followed you.

537
01:02:37,154 --> 01:02:39,864
Don't you understand stil?

538
01:02:40,264 --> 01:02:43,624
We don't want your favour, Dundar bey.

539
01:02:44,073 --> 01:02:46,373
If you had killed us with your gun....

540
01:02:46,543 --> 01:02:50,543
....you would be a little bit
precious for us.

541
01:02:51,590 --> 01:02:56,230
But now, there is some words in front
of our eyes.

542
01:02:57,189 --> 01:02:59,829
Victory....

543
01:02:59,829 --> 01:03:03,829
...or death.

544
01:03:09,289 --> 01:03:12,599
Our brave men have been killed
because of you.

545
01:03:12,789 --> 01:03:15,549
When will you stop allowing
your brothers to be killed?

546
01:03:15,813 --> 01:03:16,973
When?

547
01:03:17,692 --> 01:03:20,032
They are martyr, martyr!

548
01:03:20,704 --> 01:03:23,334
But the others like you
don't understand it.

549
01:03:23,423 --> 01:03:25,453
They don't know, Dündar bey.

550
01:03:33,338 --> 01:03:34,638
Samsa bey.

551
01:03:35,706 --> 01:03:36,986
Bamsı bey.

552
01:03:38,261 --> 01:03:40,501
What kind of a seigniory it is?

553
01:03:40,521 --> 01:03:42,481
What kind of a seigniory it is?

554
01:03:42,630 --> 01:03:46,630
How we will pay the cost of
all dead Mongols?

555
01:03:46,829 --> 01:03:49,869
We'll pay the cost with the
blood of our martyrs.

556
01:03:50,030 --> 01:03:52,470
We will not allow such traitors
like you...

557
01:03:52,708 --> 01:03:56,788
...to break into the homeland
that my father conquered.

558
01:04:20,327 --> 01:04:21,477
Soldiers!

559
01:04:23,139 --> 01:04:24,609
Kill all of them.

560
01:04:46,627 --> 01:04:48,137
Don't force me!

561
01:04:48,250 --> 01:04:49,440
Don't.

562
01:05:28,182 --> 01:05:29,802
I told you don't force!

563
01:05:29,998 --> 01:05:31,468
Don't!

564
01:06:07,956 --> 01:06:09,236
Boran.

565
01:06:09,416 --> 01:06:10,806
Follow Dundar bey.

566
01:06:11,126 --> 01:06:12,416
Eyvallah, (okay) my Bey

567
01:08:59,021 --> 01:09:00,991
It seems that he went this way.

568
01:09:01,454 --> 01:09:02,754
Let's hurry.

569
01:09:02,859 --> 01:09:03,759
Come on!

570
01:09:20,870 --> 01:09:22,300
Alisar Bey!

571
01:09:22,612 --> 01:09:23,732
You, huh?

572
01:09:24,031 --> 01:09:27,241
I know you need help.
Come here.

573
01:09:38,055 --> 01:09:39,235
Run, Melik.

574
01:09:40,716 --> 01:09:44,826
Osman should follow you instead of Batur,
you can lose yourself near the river.

575
01:11:12,122 --> 01:11:13,572
This is not Batur's trace.

576
01:11:18,721 --> 01:11:20,151
This is someone else.

577
01:11:20,516 --> 01:11:21,686
Who that might be?

578
01:11:22,777 --> 01:11:24,617
Batur...

579
01:11:33,914 --> 01:11:35,884
We don't have any
casualty, fortunately.

580
01:11:36,103 --> 01:11:38,233
And Boran brother is after Dündar Bey.

581
01:11:38,722 --> 01:11:41,062
I will have him one way
or another, Dumrul.

582
01:11:42,188 --> 01:11:43,648
One way or another.

583
01:11:44,180 --> 01:11:45,030
Come on.

584
01:12:07,179 --> 01:12:08,569
Stop!

585
01:12:16,765 --> 01:12:21,005
What is it, did my banner
lord fell from his horse?

586
01:12:21,582 --> 01:12:24,452
Osman, Osman.

587
01:12:29,791 --> 01:12:31,351
What about Osman?

588
01:12:31,408 --> 01:12:34,668
Osman attacked your base.

589
01:12:35,391 --> 01:12:40,641
He killed all of your soldiers.
And now he is after my son.

590
01:12:40,793 --> 01:12:43,883
Let me go and track
him with your soldiers.

591
01:12:47,692 --> 01:12:49,572
Do you listen to what you say?

592
01:12:49,968 --> 01:12:54,878
You've heard it, let me go and
track my son with your soldiers!

593
01:12:57,904 --> 01:13:00,644
Soldiers! Go after Osman!

594
01:13:00,904 --> 01:13:04,154
Dündar bey will lead you to him, hurry!

595
01:13:04,540 --> 01:13:08,730
Balgay, where is Gündüz?
Why did you kidnap my nephew?

596
01:13:09,368 --> 01:13:10,728
What do you want from him?

597
01:13:12,209 --> 01:13:15,789
He was the one who informed
Geyhatu about Genghis Khan's laws.

598
01:13:16,204 --> 01:13:20,204
Betraying me ends with death, Dündar Bey.

599
01:13:24,183 --> 01:13:25,463
Osman Bey!

600
01:13:32,734 --> 01:13:33,784
Let's go!

601
01:13:50,017 --> 01:13:52,317
Gündüz... My nephew...

602
01:14:39,009 --> 01:14:41,759
I hope you are aware of your doings.

603
01:14:45,744 --> 01:14:47,404
Keep your heads up.

604
01:14:48,364 --> 01:14:49,804
I said keep your heads up.

605
01:14:52,930 --> 01:14:58,590
Answer me, why would you
follow tyrants' words, why?

606
01:15:01,410 --> 01:15:02,690
We were scared, my Bey.

607
01:15:07,301 --> 01:15:12,321
Brave ones die once, but
cowards die every day, Şahin Bey!

608
01:15:16,813 --> 01:15:19,973
Kayı's Beys are always strong.

609
01:15:20,588 --> 01:15:23,078
Standing strong, honorable.

610
01:15:31,451 --> 01:15:35,451
Now, know this well...

611
01:15:35,838 --> 01:15:37,498
... and hear it.

612
01:15:42,238 --> 01:15:47,648
We are inside the nest of those
tyrants that you sold Kayı's dignity to.

613
01:15:50,459 --> 01:15:55,139
Do you think we are just
babbling and fighting for nothing?

614
01:15:57,263 --> 01:16:03,093
This fight is a fight between right and
wrong, between oppressed and tyrant!

615
01:16:04,602 --> 01:16:08,392
Traps that plan to
imprison Turks exploded!

616
01:16:09,974 --> 01:16:14,364
I will make the world hear that
the Turks won't surrender!

617
01:16:15,636 --> 01:16:22,556
I will swear on my black sword, I will take
the sky as my tent, and the sun as my banner!

618
01:16:22,792 --> 01:16:26,942
My wrath will be doom for tyrants,
but hope for the oppressed!

619
01:16:27,053 --> 01:16:31,053
Allahu Akbar!

620
01:16:42,638 --> 01:16:46,638
My Osman, what will you do with them?

621
01:16:48,595 --> 01:16:57,885
Let them go to the Tent, but if you come
to me again like this, I won't forgive you.

622
01:16:59,221 --> 01:17:00,361
My Bey.

623
01:17:01,379 --> 01:17:05,679
Balgay is coming here, they are crowded.

624
01:17:15,558 --> 01:17:18,878
We've prepared such a greeting for him...

625
01:17:19,676 --> 01:17:20,796
He'll see.

626
01:17:21,544 --> 01:17:22,574
He'll see.

627
01:17:23,958 --> 01:17:24,838
Come on.

628
01:18:09,272 --> 01:18:11,232
What do you want from me, Alişar?

629
01:18:12,948 --> 01:18:16,658
I rescued you from Osman,
isn't that enough?

630
01:18:17,260 --> 01:18:20,660
You no longer reign over these lands.

631
01:18:21,527 --> 01:18:25,257
And you no longer have
power on me, Alişar.

632
01:18:28,505 --> 01:18:30,345
I have no power, huh?

633
01:18:32,754 --> 01:18:36,884
Do you think your father
reigns over these lands?

634
01:18:41,157 --> 01:18:48,957
Speak before knowing that your father
owes his banner lordship to your mother!

635
01:18:49,223 --> 01:18:50,443
What did you say?

636
01:19:00,030 --> 01:19:06,540
If your mother hadn't have sold her soul
to Balgay, your father would have nothing!

637
01:19:06,728 --> 01:19:07,838
You are lying!

638
01:19:07,977 --> 01:19:13,087
Your mother gave up Bala Hatun
to save you from Osman.

639
01:19:13,252 --> 01:19:16,532
Then Gündüz Bey, to save your father.

640
01:19:17,703 --> 01:19:22,323
She lied, saying that Gündüz Bey talked
to Geyhatu about Genghis Khan's laws.

641
01:19:23,016 --> 01:19:27,016
- How do you know all this?
- I have big ears, don't you know?

642
01:19:27,469 --> 01:19:31,959
I have eyes and ears everywhere,
haven't you learned by now?

643
01:19:34,169 --> 01:19:40,909
Gündüz Bey was valiant enough to
sacrifice himself for his Tent's Bey.

644
01:19:41,146 --> 01:19:44,926
He didn't say a word to
Balgay, he didn't snitch.

645
01:19:45,511 --> 01:19:51,331
But your father, oh, your
miserable, coward father.

646
01:19:58,958 --> 01:20:00,558
I came here as a friend.

647
01:20:15,354 --> 01:20:17,004
What do you want from me, Alişar?

648
01:20:19,152 --> 01:20:23,872
Where is Bala Hatun?
Tell me, and we are even.

649
01:20:24,210 --> 01:20:29,390
Return to your Tent, and see
the truth for yourself.

650
01:20:36,344 --> 01:20:37,994
I am asking you one last time.

651
01:20:41,238 --> 01:20:42,898
Where is Bala Hatun?

652
01:20:44,852 --> 01:20:47,772
I don't know where Bala Hatun is.

653
01:20:48,665 --> 01:20:50,475
I don't owe you anything.

654
01:20:58,051 --> 01:21:00,491
If you are a son of Bey.

655
01:21:02,653 --> 01:21:03,963
Die like one.

656
01:21:06,676 --> 01:21:10,676
Osman is an enemy of your
father because of you.

657
01:21:11,582 --> 01:21:15,722
And now, Dündar will be an
enemy of Osman because of you.

658
01:21:16,151 --> 01:21:18,371
They will fight each other.

659
01:21:19,347 --> 01:21:25,267
Then, Geyhatu will deal with Balgay.

660
01:21:26,595 --> 01:21:30,595
I will make all of my
enemies fight each other.

661
01:22:10,657 --> 01:22:12,477
Wait until things are quiet.

662
01:22:14,152 --> 01:22:17,532
Leave this dog's corpse
near the Tent by morning.

663
01:22:18,377 --> 01:22:22,377
Let my banner lordship
bathe in brothers' blood.

664
01:23:11,659 --> 01:23:14,389
Calm down, are you okay?

665
01:23:15,246 --> 01:23:17,406
Water- Do you have water, brother?

666
01:23:18,121 --> 01:23:21,311
Your brother would penetrate
mountains to get water to you.

667
01:23:21,520 --> 01:23:28,160
You were like this when you were little,
when you want something, you would-

668
01:23:55,794 --> 01:23:56,894
Idiot.

669
01:26:29,635 --> 01:26:35,055
Erlik Han, send me your wrath
from the realm of spirits!

670
01:26:48,647 --> 01:26:49,847
Erlik Han!

671
01:26:51,933 --> 01:26:57,653
I said, "Let Osman come to me".

672
01:26:59,837 --> 01:27:06,947
" Let Osman come, so this black
soil would taste his blood", I said!

673
01:27:07,312 --> 01:27:14,982
" Let him come, so that this blue sky
would taste his dying breath", I said!

674
01:27:20,056 --> 01:27:32,966
Erlik Han, either take my
life, or give me Osman!

675
01:28:13,838 --> 01:28:14,748
Up.

676
01:28:24,444 --> 01:28:26,844
While Osman attacking my Tent...

677
01:28:30,731 --> 01:28:32,781
... what were you doing?

678
01:28:42,179 --> 01:28:44,259
Cerkutay...

679
01:28:56,117 --> 01:28:59,337
What were you doing Cerkutay?

680
01:29:00,910 --> 01:29:03,630
They were crowded, Balgay.

681
01:29:03,643 --> 01:29:06,453
Samsa's Alps joined with them.

682
01:29:14,102 --> 01:29:19,412
Erlik Han, give me Osman.

683
01:29:19,492 --> 01:29:22,952
Erlik Han!

684
01:29:43,993 --> 01:29:45,863
Bala!

685
01:29:59,225 --> 01:30:04,075
I was going to ask how you are, but
I no longer need to, as I saw Sofia.

686
01:30:04,101 --> 01:30:06,481
Masha Allah (praise be), you are fine.

687
01:30:07,540 --> 01:30:11,680
- I am fine, thank Lord.
- There's something that you're not telling.

688
01:30:13,310 --> 01:30:14,930
Tell me.

689
01:30:16,757 --> 01:30:19,607
I'd destroy the mountains for you.

690
01:30:22,984 --> 01:30:27,084
I don't want anything else than
getting over these days.

691
01:30:27,119 --> 01:30:31,589
- Gonca is waiting, I should help her.
- You are not telling me.

692
01:30:32,360 --> 01:30:36,291
You are keeping away.
You ignore me.

693
01:30:37,381 --> 01:30:40,281
This is not right, Bala.

694
01:30:40,803 --> 01:30:43,583
Is it possible to ignore you?

695
01:30:45,871 --> 01:30:48,461
Just let me be with myself for a while.

696
01:31:55,261 --> 01:31:57,638
Inform Konya immediately.

697
01:31:57,638 --> 01:31:59,680
I want new soldiers.

698
01:31:59,680 --> 01:32:07,010
If they are fools like you, I will kill
them before Osman.

699
01:32:42,137 --> 01:32:47,167
Did Söğüt's air poison you too, Kongar?

700
01:32:47,302 --> 01:32:51,333
Samsa was in my hands...

701
01:32:51,333 --> 01:32:54,186
Osman and his alps catched just in time,
Commander Balgay.

702
01:32:54,186 --> 01:32:55,596
Shut up!

703
01:32:57,579 --> 01:33:02,787
- You have failed!
- They were crowded, Commander Balgay.

704
01:33:02,787 --> 01:33:05,517
We couldn't understand where they
came from.

705
01:33:06,054 --> 01:33:09,608
Don't ever come with excuses again.

706
01:33:09,608 --> 01:33:11,588
Never!

707
01:33:16,499 --> 01:33:20,409
How did you escape, tell me.

708
01:33:22,932 --> 01:33:28,912
You know, Commander Balgay.
There is no chain to hold me.

709
01:33:31,125 --> 01:33:34,785
- Are they located?
- They took precautions.

710
01:33:34,827 --> 01:33:40,154
They took Sofia and me to different
places. They use the whole forest.

711
01:33:40,154 --> 01:33:43,114
It's impossible to find Osman.

712
01:34:04,516 --> 01:34:07,986
Commander Balgay, Alişar has come.

713
01:34:08,734 --> 01:34:10,544
Let him in the tribe.

714
01:34:11,420 --> 01:34:17,080
Go and prepare.
We will take Osman's life tomorrow.

715
01:35:20,738 --> 01:35:24,668
What's new, Konur?
What are you doing here?

716
01:35:26,117 --> 01:35:28,317
Where is Kongar?

717
01:35:33,190 --> 01:35:36,050
I am telling you, don't you hear me?

718
01:35:38,633 --> 01:35:41,553
My Bey, Kongar escaped.

719
01:35:43,309 --> 01:35:45,739
What do you mean?

720
01:35:49,280 --> 01:35:53,633
What do you mean?
Didn't I tell you to keep an eye on him?

721
01:35:53,633 --> 01:35:55,563
Didn't I?

722
01:35:56,451 --> 01:35:59,871
Water, my Bey.
He wanted water.

723
01:36:00,901 --> 01:36:05,207
While I was pouring water into the bowl,
he hit my head in the back.

724
01:36:05,207 --> 01:36:08,527
Didn't you tie him after we left?

725
01:36:08,605 --> 01:36:11,935
- Didn't you?!
- I didn't, my Bey.

726
01:36:22,618 --> 01:36:24,928
Get up!

727
01:36:25,335 --> 01:36:29,765
You failed the mission, at least stand up
in front of me.

728
01:36:48,888 --> 01:36:52,148
Kill me, my Bey, kill me.

729
01:36:52,575 --> 01:36:57,735
Why didn't you tie Kongar?
Why didn't you take precautions?

730
01:37:00,325 --> 01:37:04,210
I can't tell you, my Bey.

731
01:37:06,056 --> 01:37:11,562
What can't you tell, Konur?
What is it?

732
01:37:11,562 --> 01:37:14,772
What can't you tell, Konur?!

733
01:37:23,825 --> 01:37:26,765
You'll make me kill my company.

734
01:37:28,101 --> 01:37:31,761
- Get out of my sight!
- I won't!

735
01:37:32,411 --> 01:37:38,011
I will not go anywhere.
I won't leave you even if you kill me!

736
01:37:38,159 --> 01:37:42,161
Then why didn't you tie Kongar, ha?

737
01:37:43,011 --> 01:37:48,771
Kongar is my lost brother Göktuğ.

738
01:38:18,739 --> 01:38:21,899
What news did you bring me from Konya?

739
01:38:24,424 --> 01:38:27,414
I couldn't go to Geyhatu.

740
01:38:27,423 --> 01:38:31,113
However, I heard everything in the palace.

741
01:38:38,259 --> 01:38:39,549
Talk.

742
01:38:39,619 --> 01:38:45,919
Geyhatu knows Osman killed his
servant Köni. He went mad.

743
01:38:46,157 --> 01:38:49,334
He turned the palace upside down.

744
01:38:49,334 --> 01:38:55,224
They say, he couldn't stop and killed one
of Sultan's sons.

745
01:38:56,185 --> 01:39:01,154
However, they say, if you don't take
care of Osman and take the laws...

746
01:39:01,154 --> 01:39:05,954
Geyhatu will call you to account.

747
01:39:06,379 --> 01:39:09,699
He sent a scout troop to find Osman.

748
01:39:09,917 --> 01:39:13,017
They will arrive here as soon as possible.

749
01:39:19,828 --> 01:39:23,809
Doesn't Geyhatu trust me?

750
01:39:23,809 --> 01:39:29,689
There are many who think you took
Cengiz Han's laws for yourself, Balgay.

751
01:39:30,388 --> 01:39:35,158
However, gossips keep coming.

752
01:39:37,198 --> 01:39:41,491
- I don't know what he is thinking.
- Shut up!

753
01:39:41,491 --> 01:39:45,191
Protect yourself from Geyhatu's anger,
Balgay.

754
01:39:46,720 --> 01:39:52,630
I have come from a long way, if you
allow me...

755
01:39:53,415 --> 01:39:55,245
I want to rest.

756
01:39:55,265 --> 01:39:57,950
I have important things to do tomorrow.

757
01:39:58,100 --> 01:40:03,390
When you return, I will have
new orders for you.

758
01:40:11,356 --> 01:40:14,576
I heard that you gave the banner lordship
to Dündar Bey.

759
01:40:14,584 --> 01:40:17,124
Until I am done with him.

760
01:40:18,509 --> 01:40:20,669
Go.

761
01:40:55,491 --> 01:40:59,741
Thank Lord, Allah gave you to us, brother.

762
01:41:01,507 --> 01:41:04,587
- Gündüz
- Aunt.

763
01:41:05,673 --> 01:41:07,853
Ayşe.

764
01:41:14,076 --> 01:41:16,306
What are you doing here?

765
01:41:16,696 --> 01:41:18,568
How did you come?

766
01:41:18,568 --> 01:41:23,088
Osman brought me.
I couldn't wait you in the tribe.

767
01:41:23,632 --> 01:41:26,412
Gündüz, what did they do to you?

768
01:41:28,294 --> 01:41:30,564
Don't think about it.

769
01:41:33,822 --> 01:41:36,962
My brother saved me.

770
01:41:37,760 --> 01:41:41,830
From now on, we will take care of it.

771
01:41:43,600 --> 01:41:46,830
May Allah give you the best, Osman.

772
01:41:46,840 --> 01:41:54,310
May Allah give best to hatuns and
men who support us in this war, Aunt.

773
01:42:00,438 --> 01:42:04,178
I would
never give my brother to those ignobles.

774
01:42:11,553 --> 01:42:15,343
- Welcome, Hatun.
- Thank you.

775
01:42:17,705 --> 01:42:21,965
- May Allah heal you, Gündüz Bey.
- Eyvallah (thank you)

776
01:42:24,539 --> 01:42:26,199
Osman Bey.

777
01:42:27,282 --> 01:42:29,062
Come with me.

778
01:42:29,193 --> 01:42:31,593
I have something to tell you.

779
01:42:45,788 --> 01:42:48,488
Don't worry.
I am fine.

780
01:42:50,454 --> 01:42:52,494
Thank Lord.

781
01:42:55,120 --> 01:42:59,530
I will say it directly, Osman Bey.

782
01:43:00,903 --> 01:43:04,323
Our fellowship will continue on the war.

783
01:43:05,522 --> 01:43:08,462
But don't expect me more.

784
01:43:16,895 --> 01:43:19,695
I won't give up unless you tell me
the reason, Bala.

785
01:43:22,097 --> 01:43:30,297
I was grown for these days. My mission
is to stand by my father.

786
01:43:33,419 --> 01:43:36,879
I understand that love is not for me.

787
01:43:46,515 --> 01:43:49,425
Why are you telling me this, Bala?

788
01:43:53,254 --> 01:43:58,784
There is something else, there is
something else you are hiding.

789
01:43:59,263 --> 01:44:01,713
This is all.

790
01:44:05,316 --> 01:44:07,836
Look for another Hatun for yourself.

791
01:44:10,304 --> 01:44:13,304
I am no good for you, Osman Bey.

792
01:44:16,748 --> 01:44:19,578
I am under your command anytime.

793
01:44:20,316 --> 01:44:22,606
May Allah ease your way.

794
01:44:44,157 --> 01:44:46,537
Why is my father late, mother?

795
01:44:46,547 --> 01:44:50,877
Don't panic, Aygül. Set the table.
Your father will come any time now.

796
01:44:54,359 --> 01:44:57,319
- Father.
- My Bey.

797
01:44:58,436 --> 01:45:01,026
What happened to you, my Bey?

798
01:45:07,866 --> 01:45:09,786
Osman...

799
01:45:10,229 --> 01:45:14,799
Osman raided Balgay's base.
He wanted to kill me and Batur.

800
01:45:15,039 --> 01:45:17,369
He killed our Alps.

801
01:45:19,012 --> 01:45:23,509
- Where is Batur, Dündar Bey?
- Osman is chasing Batur.

802
01:45:23,509 --> 01:45:28,849
We searched in everywhere with soldiers.
But we couldn't find any traces.

803
01:45:29,357 --> 01:45:31,287
My son...

804
01:45:32,543 --> 01:45:35,773
My Osman went to get his brother,
obviously.

805
01:45:38,279 --> 01:45:43,054
You're being a banner lord for the dog who
kidnapped Gündüz Bey and killed your Alps...

806
01:45:43,104 --> 01:45:45,977
Then you accuse Osman!

807
01:45:45,977 --> 01:45:49,772
Enough!
Get out of our tribe, Hatun, get out!

808
01:45:49,772 --> 01:45:53,072
When did this tribe become your tribe,
Hatun?

809
01:45:54,102 --> 01:45:59,062
Selcan Hatun, get out of here before
I do something wrong.

810
01:46:00,124 --> 01:46:05,824
First Bala Hatun, now Gündüz.
There's a huge hole in your tribe, Dündar!

811
01:46:06,883 --> 01:46:11,073
Do you think what you talk here
stays here?

812
01:46:11,181 --> 01:46:14,961
What you talk goes to Balgay's ears!
Don't you understand?

813
01:46:14,966 --> 01:46:19,056
What do you mean?
Say what you are going to say!

814
01:46:19,250 --> 01:46:22,187
What I mean is obvious...

815
01:46:22,187 --> 01:46:26,441
I came here to tell you that Ayşe Hatun
is not in her tent, but now I understand...

816
01:46:26,441 --> 01:46:30,561
that my Osman took Ayşe Hatun to Gündüz.

817
01:46:31,231 --> 01:46:33,808
What comes around goes around.

818
01:46:33,808 --> 01:46:43,059
The day which we call you, not Osman,
to account for our Alps' blood is coming!

819
01:46:47,629 --> 01:46:50,489
You don't have heart to hit me.

820
01:46:51,920 --> 01:46:56,290
Hatun, Hatun get out of here.

821
01:46:56,318 --> 01:46:58,498
Get out!

822
01:46:58,718 --> 01:47:00,278
Get out.

823
01:47:00,278 --> 01:47:04,165
The tribe and the tradition is ours.

824
01:47:04,165 --> 01:47:08,199
Don't underestimate anyone, Dündar.

825
01:47:08,199 --> 01:47:12,639
Everyone is on guard.

826
01:47:16,572 --> 01:47:18,312
Saltug!

827
01:47:20,333 --> 01:47:25,583
Prepare Alps immediately.
We will set off to search Batur Bey.

828
01:47:26,143 --> 01:47:29,716
We won't come back before
killing Osman.

829
01:47:29,716 --> 01:47:31,906
As you order, my Bey.

830
01:48:12,616 --> 01:48:14,616
My Osman.

831
01:48:17,913 --> 01:48:22,273
My Osman, come, come.

832
01:48:31,403 --> 01:48:35,563
My Osman, what does bother you?

833
01:48:37,225 --> 01:48:42,205
Does betrayal or the enemy bother you?

834
01:48:43,262 --> 01:48:48,862
Neither betrayal nor the enemy bothers
me.

835
01:48:56,007 --> 01:48:58,677
The fire is in my heart, Bamsı Bey.

836
01:49:03,915 --> 01:49:06,015
In my heart.

837
01:49:07,785 --> 01:49:15,345
My Osman, if you think of Sheik Edebalı's
willing, don't worry.

838
01:49:16,115 --> 01:49:22,696
Edebalı is a mighty person.
He is waiting for the right time, my Osman.

839
01:49:23,940 --> 01:49:25,580
No.

840
01:49:32,676 --> 01:49:35,836
It is not Edebalı that bothers me.

841
01:49:39,364 --> 01:49:41,354
It's Bala.

842
01:49:45,960 --> 01:49:48,340
She said...

843
01:49:49,141 --> 01:49:51,661
She said she doesn't want me.

844
01:49:53,751 --> 01:49:56,981
First, her father despised me.

845
01:49:59,501 --> 01:50:01,601
Now, the girl.

846
01:50:01,638 --> 01:50:03,599
Now the girl despises me.

847
01:50:03,599 --> 01:50:07,599
My Osman, why do you think like that?

848
01:50:08,952 --> 01:50:12,282
Don't set your mind like that.

849
01:50:15,652 --> 01:50:20,902
It is not my decision.
Bala decided that, Bamsı Bey.

850
01:50:22,926 --> 01:50:25,976
She has a point, actually.

851
01:50:26,491 --> 01:50:30,141
We are in a path that we don't
know what will happen tomorrow.

852
01:50:30,346 --> 01:50:36,976
So, so, standing by my side has
crushed her.

853
01:50:38,825 --> 01:50:40,895
It's been much.

854
01:50:41,080 --> 01:50:47,190
Son, I know my daughter Bala.
I know my daughter Bala.

855
01:50:47,356 --> 01:50:52,576
She is neither worried of tomorrow, nor
escapes from the difficulty.

856
01:50:53,067 --> 01:50:59,587
Son, do not worry because of
some void reasons.

857
01:50:59,961 --> 01:51:03,961
The heart carries love and the
patience carries the heart.

858
01:51:04,253 --> 01:51:07,343
The love thing is complicated.

859
01:51:13,458 --> 01:51:16,008
My Osman...

860
01:51:17,277 --> 01:51:19,637
I think...

861
01:51:20,394 --> 01:51:25,174
there's something wrong in this
and it will come out soon.

862
01:51:30,546 --> 01:51:32,736
My Osman.

863
01:51:32,979 --> 01:51:37,199
Waiting is the faith of lovers, Osman.

864
01:51:39,630 --> 01:51:42,960
Be patient.

865
01:51:43,115 --> 01:51:45,895
Be patient, son.

866
01:52:10,142 --> 01:52:11,912
It's because of me.

867
01:52:13,387 --> 01:52:15,457
It's because of me.

868
01:52:17,791 --> 01:52:19,681
It's because of me.

869
01:52:28,569 --> 01:52:30,219
It's because of me.

870
01:52:47,373 --> 01:52:49,173
Konur Alp...

871
01:52:50,791 --> 01:52:52,671
what are you saying?

872
01:52:56,228 --> 01:52:58,628
I'm saying...

873
01:53:00,599 --> 01:53:01,779
I'm saying...

874
01:53:01,857 --> 01:53:03,727
I'm---

875
01:53:04,505 --> 01:53:06,435
He's my brother.

876
01:53:06,790 --> 01:53:09,310
What can I say, Sergeant Samsa?

877
01:53:13,412 --> 01:53:15,942
You've done what's necessary.

878
01:53:21,587 --> 01:53:25,357
I wouldn't forgive you if
you killed your brother.

879
01:53:27,787 --> 01:53:29,687
It's brotherhood.

880
01:53:49,384 --> 01:53:53,944
My brother Alabörü was
martyred in Mongol raid.

881
01:53:56,086 --> 01:53:57,866
In front of my eyes...

882
01:54:00,936 --> 01:54:03,356
I wish he was alive.

883
01:54:09,833 --> 01:54:14,233
I would return him to self by
hitting with my own hands.

884
01:54:17,313 --> 01:54:19,403
I wish he was breathing.

885
01:54:28,864 --> 01:54:31,564
Alabörü is dead now.

886
01:54:33,236 --> 01:54:37,506
I can only pray for him.

887
01:54:41,536 --> 01:54:43,676
But you can do other things.

888
01:54:44,920 --> 01:54:47,110
Protect your brother.

889
01:54:47,468 --> 01:54:49,618
We're with you.

890
01:54:49,864 --> 01:54:52,144
He doesn't believe me, Samsa Bey.

891
01:54:52,657 --> 01:54:54,747
He doesn't believe me.

892
01:54:56,807 --> 01:54:58,087
Konur...

893
01:54:58,714 --> 01:55:01,124
Then why didn't he kill you?

894
01:55:10,514 --> 01:55:13,194
He believes you.

895
01:55:17,831 --> 01:55:20,131
Don't worry, Konur.

896
01:55:20,743 --> 01:55:24,743
Göktuğ is the son of a brave mother
and father.

897
01:55:25,626 --> 01:55:28,106
He has compassion in his heart.

898
01:55:28,844 --> 01:55:31,424
As long as he has it...

899
01:55:32,330 --> 01:55:34,980
it will be a hope for us.

900
01:55:37,010 --> 01:55:39,630
Thank you, Sergeant Samsa.

901
01:55:40,634 --> 01:55:42,614
Thank you.

902
01:55:49,422 --> 01:55:50,922
Thank you.

903
01:55:57,340 --> 01:55:59,690
Are the soldiers deployed?

904
01:55:59,690 --> 01:56:03,690
They are deployed in the place you said.

905
01:56:04,070 --> 01:56:06,620
What is our route?

906
01:56:06,683 --> 01:56:11,923
Here. We'll climb over Kurtlar Hill.

907
01:56:12,458 --> 01:56:15,648
In which route do the soldiers go?

908
01:56:15,700 --> 01:56:19,490
From here. The other way is long and...

909
01:56:19,686 --> 01:56:21,756
spook.

910
01:56:22,666 --> 01:56:25,686
Then we...

911
01:56:26,048 --> 01:56:28,888
will go to Kurtlar Hill.

912
01:56:33,370 --> 01:56:39,430
How can you set a trap for me
with your lame brain, Osman?

913
01:56:41,896 --> 01:56:47,676
You won't save yourself this time.

914
01:56:57,740 --> 01:57:01,430
I told Yannis that I'd set a
trap in İnegöl border.

915
01:57:01,876 --> 01:57:05,496
But the war is full of tricks.

916
01:57:05,717 --> 01:57:08,117
We won't set the trap in there.

917
01:57:08,686 --> 01:57:09,986
We'll set it in...

918
01:57:11,150 --> 01:57:13,700
Kurtlar Hill.

919
01:57:15,396 --> 01:57:19,256
Balgay's base is far from there.

920
01:57:20,201 --> 01:57:23,221
They won't think that the trap is there.

921
01:57:24,489 --> 01:57:26,469
They will be unprepared.

922
01:57:26,916 --> 01:57:29,976
If Yannis told them where the trap is...

923
01:57:30,303 --> 01:57:32,203
they may be prepared.

924
01:57:32,376 --> 01:57:37,246
Mongol soldiers already passed Kurtlar
Hill and arrived at border.

925
01:57:37,360 --> 01:57:40,590
We should've killed them.

926
01:57:40,713 --> 01:57:44,343
They're useless, Bamsı Bey.

927
01:57:44,431 --> 01:57:48,261
Balgay will use that way because they
passed that road safely.

928
01:57:50,436 --> 01:57:55,716
Then they're waiting for
us in İnegöl border.

929
01:57:55,893 --> 01:57:58,603
That's why we divide into two.

930
01:57:59,600 --> 01:58:03,560
Samsa Bey, you and your Alps will go to...

931
01:58:03,560 --> 01:58:07,300
İnegöl border.

932
01:58:08,152 --> 01:58:11,092
They've
waited too much. When you go there...

933
01:58:11,092 --> 01:58:13,592
kill them.

934
01:58:13,688 --> 01:58:16,448
Bury their bodies in their caves.

935
01:58:16,668 --> 01:58:18,958
Thank you.

936
01:58:40,666 --> 01:58:43,226
Selcan Hatun.

937
01:58:45,353 --> 01:58:47,553
You chased me out of the marquee..

938
01:58:47,553 --> 01:58:50,593
and now out of the tent?

939
01:58:53,724 --> 01:58:56,484
You'll help, Selcan Hatun.

940
01:58:58,525 --> 01:59:00,765
I will help?

941
01:59:02,939 --> 01:59:06,329
You must be prepared, Zöhre.

942
01:59:06,444 --> 01:59:08,854
What can I do?

943
01:59:09,238 --> 01:59:11,838
My Batur is still not here.

944
01:59:12,889 --> 01:59:14,959
Osman meant it.

945
01:59:15,220 --> 01:59:17,750
He'll kill him.

946
01:59:17,880 --> 01:59:20,980
Tell him not to do anything mad.

947
01:59:21,302 --> 01:59:24,782
- He'll listen to you.
- Enough!

948
01:59:24,881 --> 01:59:27,861
You keep saying "Osman this, Osman that!"

949
01:59:27,941 --> 01:59:33,271
Look at yourselves
before saying anything!

950
01:59:33,427 --> 01:59:38,227
You don't ever see what mad Osman does.

951
01:59:38,665 --> 01:59:42,295
What did he do? What did Osman do?

952
01:59:42,906 --> 01:59:45,776
Tell me what you do first.

953
01:59:45,776 --> 01:59:49,776
First Bala, then Gündüz, now Batur...
Get out!

954
01:59:49,943 --> 01:59:53,613
Go tell someone else.

955
02:00:01,324 --> 02:00:06,004
Tell Osman not to do anything mad, Hatun!
Osman should give up on his anger.

956
02:00:07,276 --> 02:00:12,776
If something happens to my Batur, then
you'll see my real face.

957
02:01:03,488 --> 02:01:05,178
Batur.

958
02:01:36,407 --> 02:01:37,677
Batur!

959
02:01:41,776 --> 02:01:42,786
Batur!

960
02:02:05,485 --> 02:02:08,095
What are you looking at?

961
02:02:09,500 --> 02:02:13,500
Get him up. Take him to infirmary.

962
02:02:22,777 --> 02:02:24,857
He's wounded, right?

963
02:02:27,489 --> 02:02:29,609
Is he badly injured?

964
02:02:31,532 --> 02:02:33,272
Where's his wound?

965
02:02:35,670 --> 02:02:38,370
His mother will take care of him.

966
02:02:39,905 --> 02:02:43,315
My Batur, my son.

967
02:02:43,515 --> 02:02:45,585
Where's your wound?

968
02:02:45,652 --> 02:02:49,652
- My Batur...
- Batur...

969
02:02:50,865 --> 02:02:52,145
My son.

970
02:02:56,398 --> 02:03:00,868
His mother will take care of him.

971
02:03:01,375 --> 02:03:05,085
His mother.. Batur... My son...

972
02:03:05,358 --> 02:03:08,478
My son... Open your eyes.

973
02:03:08,997 --> 02:03:11,997
My son, open your eyes son.

974
02:03:13,053 --> 02:03:14,913
Zöhre...

975
02:03:16,197 --> 02:03:17,197
He's gone.

976
02:03:18,547 --> 02:03:20,077
He's dead.

977
02:03:20,236 --> 02:03:23,456
No!

978
02:03:23,735 --> 02:03:27,735
No! No!

979
02:03:30,550 --> 02:03:33,100
No! Batur!

980
02:03:33,417 --> 02:03:36,427
Open your eyes, son!

981
02:03:36,932 --> 02:03:40,482
Open your beautiful eyes!

982
02:03:41,056 --> 02:03:45,056
Batur! My son!

983
02:03:45,236 --> 02:03:49,056
My son.. My son!

984
02:03:50,031 --> 02:03:54,031
Batur!

985
02:03:54,416 --> 02:03:58,416
My son! My son!

986
02:03:58,739 --> 02:04:02,739
My Batur! My Batur!

987
02:04:03,588 --> 02:04:07,588
My son...

988
02:04:13,573 --> 02:04:17,573
They killed my son, Dündar!

989
02:04:18,776 --> 02:04:22,636
My son...

990
02:04:25,175 --> 02:04:28,485
They killed my son...

991
02:04:29,778 --> 02:04:34,428
Brother... Open your eyes!

992
02:04:35,575 --> 02:04:36,545
Open your eyes.

993
02:04:36,545 --> 02:04:41,662
They killed him. They
killed my son, Dündar!

994
02:04:42,304 --> 02:04:45,634
They killed him!

995
02:04:59,868 --> 02:05:01,188
Open your eyes, brother.

996
02:05:03,561 --> 02:05:04,971
Batur...

997
02:05:07,706 --> 02:05:09,096
Brother...

998
02:05:09,914 --> 02:05:11,514
Open your eyes.

999
02:05:12,397 --> 02:05:13,647
My son.

1000
02:05:14,562 --> 02:05:15,972
My Batur.

1001
02:05:21,116 --> 02:05:22,946
My son.

1002
02:05:23,219 --> 02:05:25,539
My son...

1003
02:05:26,081 --> 02:05:27,641
Open your eyes.

1004
02:05:27,862 --> 02:05:30,912
Open your eyes, son. Your father is here.

1005
02:05:31,090 --> 02:05:34,920
Open your eyes.

1006
02:05:35,256 --> 02:05:36,586
Open your eyes.

1007
02:05:37,397 --> 02:05:40,117
Open your eyes, my Batur.

1008
02:05:40,252 --> 02:05:42,642
Brother, open your eyes.

1009
02:05:43,415 --> 02:05:46,625
- Batur...
- What did you do?

1010
02:05:47,863 --> 02:05:50,153
What did you do?

1011
02:05:55,075 --> 02:05:56,615
Osman...

1012
02:05:58,408 --> 02:06:00,898
Osman did it to my son.

1013
02:06:04,571 --> 02:06:08,221
Osman did it.

1014
02:06:08,946 --> 02:06:10,716
Open your eyes, son.

1015
02:06:16,637 --> 02:06:19,027
Alps! Alps!

1016
02:06:19,678 --> 02:06:21,778
Everyone go out of the tent!

1017
02:06:22,909 --> 02:06:25,619
Search everywhere!

1018
02:06:26,137 --> 02:06:28,687
Everyone go out of the tent!

1019
02:06:35,280 --> 02:06:36,840
Osman...

1020
02:06:37,599 --> 02:06:39,949
You'll pay for it, Osman.

1021
02:06:40,304 --> 02:06:41,644
You will.

1022
02:06:42,328 --> 02:06:45,438
I'll call you to account.

1023
02:06:46,308 --> 02:06:49,788
I will for Allah's sake!

1024
02:06:50,122 --> 02:06:53,142
I will.

1025
02:06:54,864 --> 02:06:56,054
My Batur...

1026
02:06:57,938 --> 02:07:01,368
Come on! Don't stop!

1027
02:07:02,125 --> 02:07:04,535
Come on!

1028
02:07:20,788 --> 02:07:23,168
Brother...

1029
02:07:23,829 --> 02:07:25,009
Brother....

1030
02:07:38,920 --> 02:07:41,010
Beast!

1031
02:07:42,394 --> 02:07:43,274
Mother.

1032
02:07:46,774 --> 02:07:49,814
Get out, beast!

1033
02:07:51,637 --> 02:07:54,517
You killed my son.

1034
02:07:55,564 --> 02:07:58,834
Go to where Osman is.

1035
02:08:00,267 --> 02:08:02,727
Get out, beast!

1036
02:08:04,293 --> 02:08:05,973
Beast!

1037
02:08:29,167 --> 02:08:31,487
Osman!

1038
02:08:34,156 --> 02:08:35,456
Osman.

1039
02:09:01,440 --> 02:09:02,850
It may be a trap.

1040
02:09:14,259 --> 02:09:17,539
No one knows that we'll
come here, Commander Balgay.

1041
02:09:18,398 --> 02:09:22,708
They may know, Kongar.

1042
02:09:25,454 --> 02:09:28,714
As long as the sky and the
ground is fine...

1043
02:09:29,139 --> 02:09:31,209
holy trees won't fall.

1044
02:09:31,639 --> 02:09:35,359
